/*
* Peds voice system on top level:
* Ped's model will determine "speech type":
*    GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_TYPE_GEN
*    GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_TYPE_EMG
*    GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_TYPE_PLAYER
*    GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_TYPE_GANG
*    GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_TYPE_GFD
*    GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_TYPE_SPC
*
* Ped's action/situation will determine "global speech context":
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_ARRESTED
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_BUMP
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_CAR_CRASH
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_CHAT
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_CRIMINAL_PLEAD
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_DRUGS_BUY
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_DRUGS_SELL
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_FIGHT
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_STEALTH_ALERT_GENERIC
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_ENEMY_GANG_WASTED
*   GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_PLAYER_WASTED
*
* We then need to figure out "local context"
* The gPedSpeechContextMap variable contains the mapping from global context to local context.
* The mapping formula can be said as x = global_context * speech_type_count + speech_type, for example:
*    index = GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_CONTEXT_FIGHT * 5 + GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_TYPE_EMG = 89 * 5 + 1 = 446
*    We take the value that is at gPedSpeechContextMap[446] and call it "local context"
* The "local context" can be viewed as "the type of line that someone will say", but we later need to figure out "which voice will say the line"
* The array is generated based on 'gta-reversed': https://github.com/gta-reversed/gta-reversed/blob/master/source/game_sa/Audio/Enums/PedSpeechContexts.h#L9
*
* We must also ask peds.ide for "voicemin" and "voicemax", which tells us which voices this ped model can have (usually just 1 voice per model).
*
* With our possible voices, let's pick one (voicemin).
* We use the "local context" together with the selected voice to find the possible sound IDs in the correct speech array.
* For example, for "EMG" speech type:
*   y = local_context * voice_count + voice_min; gPedSpeechEmgRanges[y]
* The array is generated based on 'gta-reversed': https://github.com/gta-reversed/gta-reversed/blob/master/source/game_sa/Audio/Entities/PedSpeechAudioEntityLUTs.inc.h#L494
* But the array contains packed values containing a "first sound id" and "last sound id". We can pick a sound ID between them.
* For example, we can pick:
*   soundId = 11
*
* When we have the sound ID, we need to get the bank ID.
* To get the bank ID, we simply use: GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_EMG_FIRST_BANK + voiceId
* For example, we can get:
*   bank 367, sample 11
*
* When we have a bank ID, we can check its range and find which "archive" contains the sound ID.
* For example:
*   bank 367 is between GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_EMG_FIRST_BANK and GTA_PEDS_IDE_SPEECH_EMG_LAST_BANK, which gives us "SPC_EA"
*
* With that we can inform the user which .wav file needs to be played
*/

